  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal, by reason of siting, mass and design, would be an undesirable addition which would create a new discordant frontage along a section of Sylvan Avenue which is characterised by its openness and would appear at odds within the rear garden setting. As such, it fails to respect or reflect the character of the host dwelling, local area and street scene along Sylvan Avenue, causing harm to each of these. The proposal thus fails to accord with the following policies which seek to ensure development proposals are well designed, suitable for the site and local context, and respect and reflect the existing character:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policies D4 of the London Plan (March 2021) Policies SP2 and DMD1 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
